
## IntelliJ run configurations:
.run/*

# VS Code settings:
.vscode/*

## Generated by gitguardian's ggshield CLI. Not worth it to exempt from every repo I run it on
.cache_ggshield

# Nothing-is-as-permanent-as-temporary - allow myself to drop these files into any repo I care to add to
.editorconfig
.sdkmanrc

# Environment configuration doesn't/shouldn't go anywhere but your local file:
**/.env

# Python generates these files when compiling .pyc files
# This is *hopefully* obviated by setting $PYTHONPYCACHEPREFIX, which stashes these into an XDG directory instead
**/__pycache__/

# Some files are just... always generated and I'd never like to consider them to be "something that could be committed"
# Work is especially egregious - the pom.xml files grab rpms from artifactory, and drops them *outside* the target folder
**.rpm

# It's probably correct to put this only in maven repos, but it's everywhere I use CI friendly variables:
**/.flattened-pom.xml

# Some repos have a /bin folder. Some of those (pyenv) have a parallel /man folder. If you run `mandb --user-db`
# while your repo's /bin folder is on the path, then it creates a local file that you probably want to always ignore
man/index.db
